WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.638
Eleven readiness checks stand between
a qualified partner and production.

2
00:00:04.638 --> 00:00:09.138
They aren't the program's phase gates;
they're specific to each relationship.

3
00:00:09.138 --> 00:00:13.337
They confirm the class and the
partner's authoritative source;

4
00:00:13.337 --> 00:00:17.619
record which requirements apply;
review the agreement, privacy,

5
00:00:17.619 --> 00:00:22.708
records and the authorization boundary;
select assurance per transaction;

6
00:00:22.708 --> 00:00:25.777
name owners and test
the escalation contacts;

7
00:00:25.777 --> 00:00:31.351
reconcile the expected population against
the accounts; minimize the attributes;

8
00:00:31.351 --> 00:00:36.197
test create, update, disable, removal,
emergency suspension and rollback;

9
00:00:36.197 --> 00:00:40.236
test access, including denials;
and confirm that monitoring,

10
00:00:40.236 --> 00:00:43.538
reviews, drift detection
and runbooks are operating.

11
00:00:43.538 --> 00:00:46.525
The eleventh is production
enablement itself.

12
00:00:46.525 --> 00:00:49.499
Each check has one decider,
the business owner,

13
00:00:49.499 --> 00:00:51.925
and the checks repeat at every review.

14
00:00:51.925 --> 00:00:55.420
A partner that adds a new
application reruns four of them.
